From 484f701813af703e3b5278fa35ab106c0544c169 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Micheal Waltz <micheal@ecliptik.com>
Date: Thu, 27 Aug 2026 08:14:37 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] dos: pump the audio ring explicitly once per frame, to a
 target depth

patch 0006 fixed Passage's cooperative-scheduler yield (SDL_Delay
instead of Thread::staticSleep), which got PlayDevice running at all
under DOSBox-X -- but per doskutsu's own real-hardware history, relying
on cooperative SDL_Delay yielding alone is gap-prone on real (non-
emulated) timing: an individual render gap can outlast the audio ring
depth even when the engine yields correctly, causing underrun
regardless of average frame rate. doskutsu hit this and fixed it with
an explicit engine-side pump (nxengine-evo/0162+), calling
SDL_DOSAudioPump() -- a real shared-backend export already vendored in
this port's own SDL (vendor/SDL/include/SDL3/SDL_dosaudio_pump.h,
"DOSKUTSU local addition... never upstreamed") -- once per frame to
top the ring up, rather than hoping the cooperative scheduler gets to
it.

First revision of this patch pumped to FULL capacity every frame
(`while (SDL_DOSAudioPump()) { }`) and confirmed audio audible on real
hardware -- but real-hardware SDLDBG.LOG from a follow-up fps
investigation showed 424 of 426 SDL_DOSAudioPump calls hitting its own
>32-iteration safety cap (a near-maximal catch-up burst almost every
single frame), a real and likely significant per-frame cost, and a much
more aggressive usage pattern than doskutsu's own reference (which
only calls this at rare stage-load seams, not every frame).

Revised to pump to a target DEPTH instead of full capacity, per
SDL_DOSAudioRingFillMs's own doc comment ("the input to the engine
depth-setpoint pump... pump SDL_DOSAudioPump() until this reaches a
target depth, clamp the target below SDL_DOSAudioRingCapacityMs()").
150ms is comfortably above one frame's audio (~67ms at Passage's
15fps target) and well under a full ring (doskutsu's own production
ring is ~372ms) -- enough safety margin without needing anywhere near
as many iterations per frame in steady state. Passage has no long
blocking I/O during gameplay (unlike doskutsu's stage-load reads, the
scenario this mechanism was built for), so a shallower target should
be sufficient.

Verified under DOSBox-X with SDL_HINT_DOS_SILENCE_HISTO=1 (an earlier
revision): PlayDevice activity fully non-silent. Real-hardware
confirmation of BOTH the audio-audibility result and the reduced
cap-trip rate is the next real-hardware round.
---
 gameSource/game.cpp | 52 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 51 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/gameSource/game.cpp b/gameSource/game.cpp
index a077fc5..c55519c 100644
--- a/gameSource/game.cpp
+++ b/gameSource/game.cpp
@@ -29,6 +29,17 @@ int main( int inArgCount, char **inArgs ) {
 
 #include <SDL3/SDL.h>
 
+#ifdef __DJGPP__
+// DOS-PORT: engine-side audio-ring pump. See SDL_dosaudio_pump.h's own
+// doc comment -- the cooperative-scheduler audio thread only runs when
+// the engine yields, and on real (non-emulated) hardware a render gap
+// can outlast the ring depth even with correct SDL_Delay/yield behavior.
+// doskutsu's own history (nxengine-evo/0162+) hit exactly this and fixed
+// it by pumping the ring explicitly once per frame rather than relying
+// on cooperative scheduling alone.
+#include <SDL3/SDL_dosaudio_pump.h>
+#endif
+
 #include "blowUp.h"
 #include "World.h"
 #include "map.h"
@@ -992,7 +1003,46 @@ char playGame() {
             
         
         flipGameImageOntoScreen( screen );
-        
+
+
+#ifdef __DJGPP__
+        // DOS-PORT: top up the audio ring explicitly once per frame,
+        // rather than relying solely on the cooperative-scheduler audio
+        // thread getting yielded to (see the SDL_dosaudio_pump.h include
+        // above). Safe to call unconditionally -- a no-op if no audio
+        // device is open.
+        //
+        // Pump to a target DEPTH, not to full capacity, per
+        // SDL_DOSAudioRingFillMs's own doc comment ("the input to the
+        // engine depth-setpoint pump... pump SDL_DOSAudioPump() until
+        // this reaches a target depth, clamp the target below
+        // SDL_DOSAudioRingCapacityMs()"). Real-hardware measurement
+        // (SDLDBG.LOG, 424/426 SDL_DOSAudioPump calls hitting its
+        // own >32-iteration safety cap) showed the naive
+        // pump-to-full-every-frame version (a prior revision of this
+        // patch) doing a near-maximal catch-up burst almost every
+        // single frame -- real, non-trivial per-frame cost, and the
+        // likely cause of a measured-slower-than-15fps regression.
+        // Passage has no long blocking I/O mid-gameplay (unlike
+        // doskutsu's stage-load reads, what this mechanism was
+        // originally built for), so a much shallower target -- comfortably
+        // above one frame's worth of audio (~67 ms at 15 fps), well
+        // under a full ring (doskutsu's own production ring is ~372 ms)
+        // -- is expected to be enough of a safety margin without
+        // pumping nearly as hard every frame.
+        {
+            const int pumpTargetMs = 150;
+            int pumpCapacityMs = SDL_DOSAudioRingCapacityMs();
+            int pumpClampedTargetMs = pumpTargetMs;
+            if( pumpCapacityMs > 0 && pumpClampedTargetMs > pumpCapacityMs ) {
+                pumpClampedTargetMs = pumpCapacityMs;
+                }
+            while( SDL_DOSAudioRingFillMs() < pumpClampedTargetMs &&
+                   SDL_DOSAudioPump() ) {
+                }
+            }
+#endif
+
 
         // done with frame
         double newTimestamp = Time::getCurrentTime();
-- 
